X	icloud-drive-local-files	li	2. **Let macOS do it as space runs out:** System Settings › your name › iCloud › Drive, check that Sync this Mac is on, turn on **Optimize Mac Storage**, and click Done. Apple says your Mac can then store documents in iCloud when more space is needed.
X	icloud-drive-local-files	li	3. **Keep some things on the Mac no matter what:** Control-click them and choose Keep Downloaded.
X	icloud-drive-local-files	li	4. **Delete for good:** only for files you don’t want anywhere. Move them to the Trash in Finder; they leave your other devices too, and iCloud.com keeps them in Recently Deleted for 30 days.
X	icloud-drive-local-files	p	Don’t delete folders inside `~/Library/Mobile Documents` to save space. That deletes the files from iCloud and from every device, not just from this Mac.
