X	node-modules	p	**Yes**, in projects you aren’t running right now. It’s the packages your package manager installed from `package.json`; none of your own code is in it.
X	node-modules	p	**What it costs you:** one install before that project runs again, which downloads or copies every package back.
X	node-modules	p	**Does it come back?** Yes, the same tree as before, when you run `npm install` (or `yarn`, `pnpm install`, `bun install`) against the project’s lockfile.
