X	bun-cache	code	bun pm cache rm
X	bun-cache	p	This deletes everything in the cache folder, the global store in `links/` included, and keeps the folder itself. Bun can’t remove a single package this way: `bun pm cache rm <package>` is an error. For one package with stale registry data, Bun’s docs suggest `bun add <pkg> --force` or `bun update <pkg>` instead of clearing.
X	bun-cache	p	One quirk: `bun pm cache rm` takes the folder from `BUN_INSTALL_CACHE_DIR`, `--cache-dir` or `BUN_INSTALL`, and ignores a cache folder named in `bunfig.toml`. If you moved the cache there, pass the same folder with `--cache-dir`.
X	bun-cache	p	Don’t delete `~/.bun` as a whole unless you mean to remove Bun: with the install script, that takes the `bun` command and your global tools with it.
