X	conda-packages	p	**Yes, through conda.** `conda clean --all` removes cached packages no environment uses, along with tarballs, index caches and logs. Deleting `pkgs` by hand can break environments that link back to it, so don’t.
X	conda-packages	p	**What it costs you:** a package removed from the cache downloads again the next time an environment needs it.
X	conda-packages	p	**Does it come back?** The cache refills as you install. Environments are different: one you remove is gone unless you exported it first.
X	conda-packages	h	Measure it
X	conda-packages	code	du -sh "$(conda info --base)"
X	conda-packages	code	du -sh "$(conda info --base)/pkgs"
