X	go-module-cache	p	**Yes**, with Go’s own commands. The module cache holds downloaded dependencies and the build cache holds compiled packages, and both come back. Use `go clean`, because module files are read-only and `rm -rf` fails on them.
X	go-module-cache	p	**What it costs you:** the next build downloads modules again and compiles from scratch.
X	go-module-cache	p	**Does it come back?** Yes. The build cache trims itself; the module cache only grows until you clean it.
X	go-module-cache	h	Measure it
X	go-module-cache	code	du -sh "$(go env GOMODCACHE)" "$(go env GOCACHE)"
X	go-module-cache	h	How to clear it
