X	go-module-cache	code	go clean -cache
X	go-module-cache	li	- `go clean -modcache` removes the entire module cache, unpacked source included. Go’s reference calls it usually the best way, because it deals with the read-only permissions for you.
X	go-module-cache	li	- `go clean -cache` removes the entire build cache.
X	go-module-cache	li	- `go clean -testcache` only expires cached test results, if stale passes are the problem.
X	go-module-cache	li	- Leave `go clean -fuzzcache` alone unless you mean it: it deletes inputs the fuzzer found that expand coverage, which makes fuzzing less effective.
X	go-module-cache	p	If you’d rather `rm -rf` worked in future, `go env -w GOFLAGS=-modcacherw` makes new module folders writable. Go’s docs ask for caution with it, since writable modules can be changed by accident; `go mod verify` detects such changes.
