X	pnpm-store	h	How to clear it
X	pnpm-store	li	1. Let any `pnpm install` that’s running finish.
X	pnpm-store	li	2. Run `pnpm store prune`. It removes unreferenced packages, those not used by any project on the system. pnpm’s docs say it has no side effects on your projects and suggest running it occasionally, not constantly.
X	pnpm-store	li	3. If you like, empty the metadata cache too. It refills on the next install.
X	pnpm-store	code	pnpm store prune
X	pnpm-store	code	rm -rf ~/Library/Caches/pnpm/*
X	pnpm-store	p	Don’t move the store in Finder or delete it while projects still use it. A project set up with pnpm’s global virtual store, which is off by default, keeps only links into the store and stops working until it’s installed again.
