X	uv-cache	p	Two commands, from gentle to complete:
X	uv-cache	li	- `uv cache prune` removes unused entries, such as ones left by earlier uv versions, and the centralized project environments uv keeps there, which it recreates when needed. uv’s docs say it’s safe to run periodically.
X	uv-cache	li	- `uv cache clean` removes every entry. `uv cache clean <package>`, for example `uv cache clean ruff`, removes only that package’s entries.
X	uv-cache	code	uv cache prune
X	uv-cache	code	uv cache clean
X	uv-cache	p	Run them while no other uv command is working. uv locks the cache while it changes it and waits up to five minutes for other uv processes; `--force` skips that wait, and is only safe when nothing else is using the cache.
