X	parallels-virtual-machines	li	4. Choose **Move to Trash** to delete it, or **Keep Files** to take it off the list and leave the bundle where it is.
X	parallels-virtual-machines	p	Only Move to Trash frees space, once you empty the Trash, and Parallels warns that the operation is irreversible.
X	parallels-virtual-machines	p	**To keep a VM but make it smaller**, Parallels suggests working through these in order: delete snapshots you no longer need in Snapshot Manager, shut down suspended VMs, then use File › Free Up Disk Space… or Reclaim in the VM’s Configuration › General. You can also turn on Reclaim disk space on shutdown, or archive a VM you rarely use from its menu in Control Center.
X	parallels-virtual-machines	p	Don’t stop a VM while Parallels is reclaiming its space: Parallels warns this can corrupt it. And if a VM has many branches of snapshots, deleting a parent snapshot can make the virtual disk bigger rather than smaller.
